#N canvas 40 60 1280 1010 12;
#X declare -path ..;
#X obj 0 0 cnv 1 1280 46 empty empty 12\ \ \ GANs\ \ -\ \ a\ forger\ and\ a\ critic\ learn\ a\ melody\ style\ (Goodfellow\ 2014) 14 23 0 20 #1d3557 #ffffff 0;
#X obj 1110 980 declare -path ..;
#X text 800 980 finds the nn.* objects one folder up ->, f 42;
#X text 20 980 neuralplay - Moisés Horta Valenzuela / SEMILLA.AI Studio, f 70;
#X text 20 56 Two networks play a game. The GENERATOR (the forger) invents pitches from noise. The DISCRIMINATOR (the critic) learns to tell its fakes from the teacher's real notes. Each one improves by beating the other \, until the forger plays in the teacher's style. Left ear: teacher. Right ear: forger., f 175;
#X obj 10 96 cnv 1 390 890 empty empty THE\ IDEA 8 12 0 13 #eef1f5 #1d3557 0;
#X text 20 122 A GENERATIVE ADVERSARIAL NETWORK (Ian Goodfellow \, 2014) never sees "the right answer". The generator only learns through the critic: it moves its output in the direction that makes the critic say "real"., f 52;
#X text 20 203 Here everything is tiny so you can read it: the generator has 2 parameters (a centre mu and a spread s: pitch = mu + s * noise) \, the critic has 3 (D(x) = sigmoid(a x + b x^2 + c) - a bump that can say "real" around some pitch range). Open [pd one-gan-step] for the five formulas., f 52;
#X text 20 314 WATCH: the critic's belief curve (lower graph) peaks where real notes are and fakes are not. The generator chases that peak. Its mean locks on quickly \, its spread wobbles - GAN training rarely sits still., f 52;
#X text 20 395 MODE COLLAPSE: switch on "two peaks". The teacher now plays in two registers \, but the forger can only make one bump: it either sits on one register (collapse) or wanders between them. Real GANs suffer from exactly this., f 52;
#X text 20 476 IN MUSIC: WaveGAN (2018) \, GANSynth (2019) generated sounds directly \, MelGAN and HiFi-GAN (2019-20) turn spectrograms into audio inside many speech and singing synthesizers. StyleGAN made faces \, the same game \, much bigger networks., f 52;
#X obj 410 96 cnv 1 860 430 empty empty WHAT\ THE\ PLAYERS\ BELIEVE\ \ (pitch\ axis:\ MIDI\ 36\ ..\ 96) 8 12 0 13 #e3f0fb #1d3557 0;
#X obj 430 130 cnv 1 600 160 empty empty empty 4 10 0 12 #ffffff #000000 0;
