#X text 20 10 After every GAN step add a little to the bins of the real and the fake pitch (0.4 / steps \, so the picture does not depend on the speed). After every note all bins fade by 10% \, and the critic curve D(pitch) is redrawn for MIDI 36..96. Array names start with a letter because [expr] reads them. Bins stop at 0.78 so a collapsed forger does not draw outside the graph., f 140;
#X obj 20 70 r \$0-hist;
#X obj 20 100 expr hr\$0[min(max(int(60 + 12 * xr_\$0 + 0.5) - 36 \, 0) \, 60)] = min(hr\$0[min(max(int(60 + 12 * xr_\$0 + 0.5) - 36 \, 0) \, 60)] + 0.4 / steps_\$0 \, 0.78) \; hf\$0[min(max(int(60 + 12 * xf_\$0 + 0.5) - 36 \, 0) \, 60)] = min(hf\$0[min(max(int(60 + 12 * xf_\$0 + 0.5) - 36 \, 0) \, 60)] + 0.4 / steps_\$0 \, 0.78), f 90;
